---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PartnerLogos from '../components/PartnerLogos.astro';
import WorkCards from '../components/WorkCards.astro';
import { homeOnlyPreview } from '../data/site';
import instruments from '../assets/images/field/latest-instruments.jpg';
import shadia from '../assets/images/field/latest-ridge.jpg';
import '../styles/about.css';
import '../styles/work.css';

const scienceHref = homeOnlyPreview ? '/#why-eclipses' : '/science';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About"
	description="Solar Wind Sherpas advances scientific understanding of the Sun through total solar eclipse expeditions, led by Dr. Shadia Habbal."
>
	<article class="page about">
		<section class="about-intro" id="introduction" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
			<div class="page-narrow">
				<p class="label page-kicker">About</p>
				<h1 id="about-heading">
					Some of the most important questions in solar physics can only be answered by going to the
					path of totality.
				</h1>
				<p class="lead">
					Thirty-one years. Twenty-one expeditions. An international collaboration led by Dr. Shadia
					Habbal.
				</p>
				<p>
					Solar Wind Sherpas organizes expeditions to total solar eclipses worldwide. Portable
					observatories go to the umbra — wherever it falls — to study the solar corona and the
					origins of the solar wind. The work is led from the Institute for Astronomy, University of
					Hawaiʻi.
				</p>
			</div>
			<figure class="about-media reveal">
				<div class="about-media-frame">
					<Image
						src={instruments}
						alt="Portable solar instruments and a field laptop on a ridge during the 2026 Burgos expedition"
						widths={[900, 1400, 2000]}
						sizes="(max-width: 1120px) 100vw, 1120px"
						loading="eager"
					/>
				</div>
				<figcaption>Burgos, Spain · 2026</figcaption>
			</figure>
		</section>

		<section class="about-block" id="our-story" aria-labelledby="story-heading">
			<div class="page-narrow">
				<h2 id="story-heading">Our Story</h2>
				<p>
					Dr. Shadia Habbal founded Solar Wind Sherpas in 1995 and has led every expedition since.
					The name is literal: each expedition carries specialised imaging systems, spectrographs,
					tracking mounts and power into the path of totality.
				</p>
			</div>
			<ol class="about-timeline">
				<li>
					<p class="about-timeline-year">1995</p>
					<p>
						The collaboration begins. The first expedition is to India, on 24 October 1995.
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p class="about-timeline-year">2005</p>
					<p>
						Dr. Habbal becomes Professor and Astronomer at the Institute for Astronomy, University
						of Hawaiʻi, where the work is based.
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p class="about-timeline-year">Today</p>
					<p>
						Thirty-one years and twenty-one expeditions, across six continents, with decades of
						peer-reviewed research on the corona and the solar wind.
					</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
		</section>

		<section class="about-block" id="people" aria-labelledby="people-heading">
			<div class="page-narrow">
				<h2 id="people-heading">The People Behind the Sherpas</h2>
				<p>
					There is no permanent roster. Each path of totality brings together the scientists,
					engineers and observers needed for those minutes. People who take part appear with that
					expedition.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="about-founder reveal">
				<figure class="about-founder-photo">
					<div class="about-founder-frame">
						<Image
							src={shadia}
							alt="Dr. Shadia Habbal in the field during the 2026 Burgos expedition"
							widths={[640, 960, 1400]}
							sizes="(max-width: 900px) 92vw, 40vw"
							class="about-founder-img"
						/>
					</div>
					<figcaption>Dr. Shadia Habbal · Burgos, Spain · 2026</figcaption>
				</figure>
				<div class="about-founder-copy">
					<p class="label">Founder</p>
					<h3>Dr. Shadia R. Habbal</h3>
					<p class="about-founder-affiliation">
						Professor and Astronomer, Institute for Astronomy, University of Hawaiʻi
					</p>
					<p>
						Dr. Shadia Rifai Habbal has spent fifty years at the frontier of solar physics. Born in
						Syria, she earned her Ph.D. in Physics from the University of Cincinnati in 1977.
					</p>
					<p>
						She spent over two decades as a Research Physicist at the Smithsonian Astrophysical
						Observatory and lectured at Harvard University. Since 2005 she has been Professor and
						Astronomer at the Institute for Astronomy, University of Hawaiʻi, and serves as Lead
						Editor of the Astrophysical Journal.
					</p>
					<p>
						Her method — deploying portable observatories to total solar eclipses — has defined her
						career. The work has been recognized with a NASA Certificate of Appreciation and an
						Honorary Doctorate from Brno University of Technology.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="home-work about-actions" id="actions" aria-labelledby="actions-heading">
			<div class="home-work-intro reveal">
				<p class="label">Actions</p>
				<h2 id="actions-heading">
					We bring solar research into the field and share the science of eclipses with the
					communities we meet.
				</h2>
			</div>
			<WorkCards outreachHref={false} />
		</section>

		<section class="about-block about-partners" id="partners" aria-labelledby="about-partners-heading">
			<div class="page-narrow">
				<h2 id="about-partners-heading">Partners & Supporters</h2>
				<p>
					Expeditions depend on institutions and supporters. The logos below are the list currently
					shown on the site. Ongoing partnerships and expedition-specific support will be
					distinguished as each relationship is confirmed.
				</p>
			</div>
			<PartnerLogos />
		</section>

		<section class="about-invite" id="invite" aria-labelledby="invite-heading">
			<div class="page-narrow">
				<p class="label">Continue</p>
				<h2 id="invite-heading">The science, or the next totality</h2>
				<p>
					Methods and papers live with the science. Support is how instruments, people and freight
					reach the path.
				</p>
				<div class="about-invite-actions">
					<a class="cta cta--button" href={scienceHref}>
						Explore the science <span class="cta-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
					</a>
					<a class="cta cta--button" href="/#support">
						Support this work <span class="cta-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
					</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
